lessons.content_markdown:
## From `desiredCapabilities` to W3C `options`

Older Appium tutorials use a flat `desiredCapabilities` object. Modern Appium (2.x) requires **W3C-compliant capabilities**, which vendor-prefix anything non-standard with `appium:`.

```js
const capabilities = {
  platformName: 'Android',
  'appium:automationName': 'UiAutomator2',
  'appium:deviceName': 'Pixel_7_API_34',
  'appium:app': '/path/to/app-debug.apk',
  'appium:autoGrantPermissions': true,
  'appium:newCommandTimeout': 240,
};
```

With WebdriverIO, these are grouped under `capabilities` in `wdio.conf.js`:
```js
exports.config = {
  hostname: 'localhost',
  port: 4723,
  path: '/',
  capabilities: [{
    platformName: 'Android',
    'appium:automationName': 'UiAutomator2',
    'appium:deviceName': 'Pixel_7_API_34',
    'appium:app': './app/app-debug.apk',
  }],
};
```

