lessons.content_markdown:
## Android-Specific Locators

```js
// By resource-id (most stable — matches Android's view IDs)
const loginBtn = await driver.$('id=com.zaka.app:id/loginButton');

// By accessibility id (cross-platform friendly)
const emailField = await driver.$('~emailInput');

// UiAutomator (Android's native selector DSL — powerful for complex matches)
const item = await driver.$(
  'android=new UiSelector().text("Wireless Mouse").className("android.widget.TextView")'
);
```

### Priority order
1. `resource-id` — fastest and most stable, assuming devs don't rename IDs carelessly
2. `accessibility id` (`~`) — also improves the app's real accessibility, a nice side benefit
3. `UiSelector` — for complex conditions (partial text, sibling relationships)
4. XPath — last resort, slow and fragile on deep view hierarchies

