lessons.content_markdown:
## `mobile:` Extension Commands

Appium exposes platform-specific power tools via `driver.execute('mobile: <command>', {...})`:

```js
// Open a deep link directly (skip navigating through the whole app)
await driver.execute('mobile: deepLink', {
  url: 'zakaapp://course/appium-mobile-automation',
  package: 'com.zaka.app',
});

// Pull down the notification shade
await driver.execute('mobile: openNotifications');

// Grant a runtime permission without a UI dialog
await driver.execute('mobile: changePermissions', {
  permissions: ['android.permission.CAMERA'],
  action: 'grant',
});
```

Deep links are especially valuable for test speed: instead of navigating five screens deep to test a feature, jump straight there and keep your test focused on the behavior you actually care about.

## iOS-Specific Locators

```js
// Accessibility id — the #1 recommended strategy on iOS
const loginBtn = await driver.$('~loginButton');

// NSPredicate string — powerful attribute-based matching
const item = await driver.$(
  '-ios predicate string:type == "XCUIElementTypeStaticText" AND label == "Wireless Mouse"'
);

// Class chain — faster alternative to XPath for hierarchical queries
const cell = await driver.$(
  '-ios class chain:**/XCUIElementTypeCell[`label == "Wireless Mouse"`]'
);
```

### Why predicate/class chain over XPath
Both are evaluated natively by XCTest (fast), whereas XPath requires Appium to build a full accessibility tree snapshot first — noticeably slower on complex screens. Reserve XPath for cases predicate strings genuinely can't express.

