lessons.content_markdown:
## Capstone Brief

Build a cross-platform Appium suite for a demo banking app covering:

1. **Biometric login simulation** (Face ID/Touch ID stub on Simulator, PIN fallback on both platforms)
2. **Cross-platform screen objects** — one test file, both Android and iOS capabilities
3. **Deep-link based test setup** — jump straight to the 'Transfer Funds' screen instead of navigating through the full app
4. **WebView handling** — the 'Statements' section is a hybrid WebView; switch context to verify a PDF download link renders
5. **CI** — run against both an Android emulator and a cloud iOS device (BrowserStack), triggered on every PR

```js
describe('Transfer funds flow', () => {
  it('completes a transfer between accounts', async () => {
    await driver.execute('mobile: deepLink', {
      url: 'zakabank://transfer',
      package: 'com.zaka.bank',
    });

    const screen = new TransferScreen(driver);
    await screen.selectFromAccount('Checking');
    await screen.selectToAccount('Savings');
    await screen.enterAmount('250.00');
    await screen.confirm();

    await expect(await screen.successBanner.getText()).toContain('Transfer complete');
  });
});
```

This capstone mirrors what a real fintech QA team builds: cross-platform coverage, fast setup via deep links, hybrid content handling, and CI-driven execution across real device coverage.

